--- Response ---
The issue has been resolved in `xarray/core/dataset.py` and `xarray/core/indexes.py`:

1. **`Dataset.reset_index` (`xarray/core/dataset.py`)**:
   - Filtered `coord_names` with `& set(variables)` so dropped coordinate variables are removed from `_coord_names` (preventing `_coord_names` from having more elements than `_variables`).
   - Used `_replace_with_new_dims` so dimensions with no remaining variables/coordinates are dropped.
   - Properly handled `PandasMultiIndex` and single indexes when resetting by dimension or level names:
     - Always drop the multi-index dimension coordinate when the multi-index itself is dropped/converted.
     - Drop or convert (`.to_base_variable()`) reset multi-index levels and single-index coordinates depending on `drop=True/False`.
     - Drop the old level coordinate variable when a multi-index is reduced to a single-level `PandasIndex` (renamed to the dimension).
2. **`Dataset.set_index` (`xarray/core/dataset.py`)**:
   - Converted de-indexed coordinate variables that are retained to base `Variable` objects via `.to_base_variable()`.
3. **`PandasMultiIndex.keep_levels` (`xarray/core/indexes.py`)**:
   - Renamed the remaining single level index to `self.dim` when a `MultiIndex` is reduced to a single `PandasIndex`.
